From cef4d90b478597e20ff105591af3c5f4417363f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hao Lin <hao.lin@samsung.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:59:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: use hybrid LLVM linkage on x86_64

Enable shared LLVM and Clang linkage in the x86_64 recipe while keeping
clang, lld and llvm-ar statically linked to LLVM components. Their driver
aliases continue to share the same executable. Other tools use libLLVM
and, where applicable, libclang-cpp through the normal upstream interfaces.

Use TIZEN_HYBRID_LINK and a per-consumer TIZEN_STATIC_LLVM property to
select component dependencies only for the three opted-in drivers.
When disabled, the shared-link interfaces retain upstream behavior.
Keep BUILD_SHARED_LIBS and the unified LLVM driver disabled on x86_64.

Preserve upstream forced-static llvm-tblgen, clang-tblgen, lldb-tblgen,
llvm-config and llvm-exegesis. Tool-private archives and build utilities
retain upstream behavior. Do not change armv7l or aarch64 recipes,
optimization flags, static-devel packaging or native archive conversion.

Validation: CMake generation with the complete x86_64 recipe parameters;
all-static, hybrid and shared controls; unchanged ARM build/install macro
expansions; clean patch application. Full build and RPM/runtime validation
are left to the receiving team.

Signed-off-by: Hao Lin <hao.lin@samsung.com>
Change-Id: I28171720d5bbbf9eaf491cdafc0aee0b43f9cd06
